# NØNOS 0.9.3: the tour, from power-on to power off, filmed by
#   tools/nonos-drive --record OUT.mp4 --steps tools/nonos_tutorial/tour.steps
# README.md beside this file has the whole command, the lanes and the timings;
# STORYBOARD.md has the chapters these sections are cut into (post/film.json).
#
# Every caption says what is on screen at that moment, and was checked
# against the code, the docs (docs/using, docs/install, docs/overview) and
# screenshots of a boot of the development image. Clicks are abs:X,Y on the
# 1920x1080 desktop, so the machine needs the usb-tablet lane; a key is used
# wherever a key does the same, because a key lands on any screen.
#
# Each app window is opened alone and closed before the next, so it opens in
# the middle of the work area (capsule_wm's cascade.rs), above the captions,
# and the positions clicked are the ones the screenshots showed.
#
# Pauses are timed for a KVM host. A wait on the machine is an until: step on
# its serial console, so a slower machine waits longer, not wrongly.
#
# Optional sections sit between a pair of marker lines; the README's sed
# line cuts any of them out:
#   market     needs the network (and, on a -dev image, the host's relay)
#   simplex    needs the listing linux.simplex-chat on main (not there yet)
#   telegram   needs the listing linux.telegram-desktop on main (not there
#              yet) and a Qt display path in the Linux personality
#   monero     needs the SOCKS endpoint on main (not there yet) and a node
#   qwen       needs a Qwen model: both images carry Qwen3 0.6B on the stick
#   dev-image  a caption true only of a -dev image
#   sealed     a caption true only of a sealed image
# Cut the one of dev-image and sealed that is not the image you film.

# ==== 1. Every boot checks itself ===========================================
say:This is NØNOS 0.9.3, from the moment the machine is switched on.
until:PCI: counted:600
pause:1
key:esc
say:The boot menu. Esc holds its countdown, so we can read each entry.
pause:6
say:Standard boots when the kernel is signed, attested and current.
pause:6
key:down
pause:1
say:Hardened also needs Secure Boot and a TPM. Here it says it would refuse.
pause:7
key:down
pause:1
key:down
pause:1
say:Air-Gapped starts no network driver and no network service at all.
pause:6
key:down
pause:1
say:Recovery is a Terminal and Files, with no network and no setup.
pause:6
key:home
pause:1
say:We start Standard.
pause:3
key:ret
say:The loader measures the kernel and checks its two signatures before it runs.
until:[SPLASH] up:600
say:The splash lists each link of the boot chain, and says what did not pass.
pause:7
say:
until:Capsules spawned:900
until:[SPLASH] stepped aside:600
pause:3

# ==== 2. No account. Thirteen answers. ======================================
say:First-boot setup: thirteen steps, all by keyboard. There is no password.
pause:6
say:Step 1, the keyboard: six layouts. Ctrl+Alt+Space cycles them at any time.
pause:6
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 2, your name, which the Terminal shows as name@host.
pause:3
type:ek
pause:3
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 3, the time zone, for the menu bar clock: j adds an hour, k takes one.
pause:3
type:j
pause:2
type:k
pause:3
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 4, the mode. Amnesic is the default: RAM only, no disk is written.
pause:7
key:down
pause:1
say:USB live cannot be chosen yet, and the screen says why.
pause:5
key:down
pause:1
say:Install to this computer keeps your answers and opens the installer.
pause:6
key:home
pause:1
say:We stay amnesic: when this machine stops, everything here is gone.
pause:5
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 5, the network. No network is the default, and the private choice.
pause:6
say:A wired card is used once a cable is in; Wi-Fi is joined only if you ask.
pause:7
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 6, the route out. The Nym mixnet is the default.
pause:5
say:It hides who you talk to, even from someone watching the whole internet.
pause:6
key:down
pause:1
say:Anyone: onion routing through three relays, much faster than the mixnet.
pause:6
say:We choose Anyone for this film. A route that fails never falls back.
pause:5
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 7, privacy: what NØNOS does without being asked. There is no telemetry.
pause:7
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 8, appearance: which wallpapers to keep, and which is the desktop's.
pause:6
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 9, the Qwen model: a language model that runs here, offline.
pause:6
say:The stick carries Qwen3 0.6B. It is held in memory, and gone at power off.
pause:7
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 10, apps: each optional app is on until you turn it off with Space.
pause:6
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 11, installed software: may programs from the Marketplace run?
pause:5
key:down
pause:1
say:We allow them, to install apps later. This machine proves each one.
pause:6
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 12, the computer's name: the host in name@host.
pause:3
type:tour
pause:3
key:ret
pause:2
say:Step 13, review every answer. Enter applies them and starts the desktop.
pause:7
key:ret
say:
until:the desktop is up:900
until:name=app.process_manager:300
pause:5

# ==== 3. Your computer forgets you; a desktop that shows its work ===========
say:A live session: nothing is kept. Files, settings and models go when it stops.
pause:7
key:esc
pause:3
say:The desktop. The dock is at the bottom, the menu bar at the top.
pause:6
